<div class="sheet-header stonetop-sheet-header">
	{{!-- The slot is what the crop pip positions against; the portrait keeps its own sizing.

	      NO data-edit: it is how ActorSheet binds Foundry's file picker to an image, and that
	      binding is registered before ours and cannot be called off from a listener — so while it
	      was here, clicking the portrait in edit mode could only ever reach the raw file browser.
	      The People of Stonetop gallery carries "Browse files…" and "Use default" of its own, so
	      it is a superset of what the attribute bought. --}}
	<span class="stonetop-portrait-slot">
		{{#if stonetop.portraitFramed}}
		{{!-- A framed portrait needs a clipping box: the image is absolutely positioned at
		      several hundred percent, so with nothing to clip it, it paints across the sheet. The
		      box wears .stonetop-portrait — it is the portrait now, and that class carries the
		      size, the border and the click that opens the window. Only this branch is new; an
		      unframed portrait stays the bare <img> it has always been, which is what lets that
		      class's own top-anchored crop go on serving everyone nobody has framed. --}}
		<span class="stonetop-portrait stonetop-portrait-clip" title="{{actor.name}}">
			<img class="stonetop-portrait-img" src="{{stonetop.portraitImg}}" style="{{stonetop.portraitImgStyle}}" alt="{{actor.name}}">
		</span>
		{{else}}
		<img class="stonetop-portrait" src="{{actor.img}}" title="{{actor.name}}" alt="{{actor.name}}">
		{{/if}}
		{{> "stonetop.portrait-frame-pip" canFrame=stonetop.canFramePortrait canTokenize=stonetop.canTokenizePortrait}}
	</span>
	<div class="sheet-header__fields">
		{{#if (and isCharacter (not limited))}}
		<div class="stonetop-playbook-block">
			<div class="stonetop-playbook-row">
				{{!-- What this character IS, in one line. Normally that's the playbook and its
				      Instinct. Once they've died and come back wearing an insert, the insert IS
				      what they are — it replaces the playbook's name here and brings its own
				      Instinct, because "Ghost (Denial)" is the true answer and "The Heavy
				      (Loyal)" is who they used to be. The old pair stays, struck through and
				      small, beside it: nothing about them was deleted, and a Revenant is still a
				      Heavy underneath. --}}
				<span class="stonetop-playbook-drop-zone {{#unless stonetop.playbook.name}}empty{{/unless}}">
					{{#if stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert}}
					{{stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.name}}{{#if stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.instinct.badge}} <span class="stonetop-instinct-badge" data-tooltip="{{stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.instinct.badge.tooltip}}" data-tooltip-direction="DOWN">({{stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.instinct.badge.word}})</span>{{/if}}
					{{else if stonetop.playbook.name}}
					{{stonetop.playbook.name}}{{#if stonetop.playbook.instinct.badge}} <span class="stonetop-instinct-badge" data-tooltip="{{stonetop.playbook.instinct.badge.tooltip}}" data-tooltip-direction="DOWN">({{stonetop.playbook.instinct.badge.word}})</span>{{/if}}
					{{else}}Drop a playbook here{{/if}}
				</span>
				{{#if stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert}}
				{{#if stonetop.playbook.name}}
				{{! The playbook goes grey the moment the insert lands — that identity IS replaced.
				    Its Instinct is a separate question and comes along only once the insert's own
				    Instinct has actually been chosen, which is the same gate the Details tab uses
				    for its "retired" note and its read-out. Between taking the insert and choosing
				    an Instinct (a state the walkthrough explicitly allows you to leave the window
				    in) the header used to strike out an Instinct the sheet was still using. }}
				<span class="stonetop-playbook-retired"
				      data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.retiredTooltip"}}" data-tooltip-direction="DOWN">
					<s>{{stonetop.playbook.name}}{{#if stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.instinct.selected}}{{#if stonetop.playbook.instinct.badge}} ({{stonetop.playbook.instinct.badge.word}}){{/if}}{{/if}}</s>
				</span>
				{{/if}}
				{{/if}}
			</div>
			{{#if stonetop.playbook.description}}
			<p class="stonetop-playbook-description">{{stonetop.playbook.description}}</p>
			{{/if}}
		</div>
		{{/if}}
		{{! The name plate, and beside it the Lightbearer's holy light. The row exists ONLY to
		    stand the candle next to the plate at the plate's own height — it is the thing this
		    character is carrying, said as loudly as their name. }}
		<div class="stonetop-name-called-row">
			<div class="stonetop-name-called-box">
				<div class="stonetop-name-called-inner">
					<span class="stonetop-name-called-label">I am called...</span>
					{{#if stonetop.editMode}}
					<input class="input--title stonetop-name-field" name="name" type="text" value="{{actor.name}}" placeholder="Name"/>
					{{else}}
					<span class="input--title stonetop-header-locked stonetop-name-field">{{actor.name}}</span>
					{{/if}}
				</div>
			</div>
			{{! Shows in BOTH edit and play mode — consecrating a flame is play, not editing — and
			    only on a sheet that can make a light (or that already has one burning, so a light
			    stranded by a playbook swap can still be snuffed). A button where the sheet is
			    editable and a span where it isn't, the same split the Dead chip below uses, so
			    nothing offers a click that would do nothing. `type="button"` is not optional: the
			    whole sheet is one <form> and a bare button submits it. }}
			{{#if stonetop.holyLight.show}}
			{{#if editable}}
			<button type="button" class="stonetop-holy-light{{#if stonetop.holyLight.lit}} is-lit{{/if}}"
			        aria-pressed="{{#if stonetop.holyLight.lit}}true{{else}}false{{/if}}"
			        aria-label="{{#if stonetop.holyLight.lit}}{{localize "stonetop.holyLight.litLabel"}}{{else}}{{localize "stonetop.holyLight.unlitLabel"}}{{/if}}"
			        data-tooltip="{{#if stonetop.holyLight.lit}}{{localize "stonetop.holyLight.litTooltip"}}{{else}}{{localize "stonetop.holyLight.unlitTooltip"}}{{/if}}"
			        data-tooltip-direction="UP"><span class="stonetop-holy-light-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
			{{else}}
			<span class="stonetop-holy-light{{#if stonetop.holyLight.lit}} is-lit{{/if}}"
			      aria-label="{{#if stonetop.holyLight.lit}}{{localize "stonetop.holyLight.litLabel"}}{{else}}{{localize "stonetop.holyLight.unlitLabel"}}{{/if}}"
			      data-tooltip="{{#if stonetop.holyLight.lit}}{{localize "stonetop.holyLight.readOnlyLit"}}{{else}}{{localize "stonetop.holyLight.readOnlyUnlit"}}{{/if}}"
			      data-tooltip-direction="UP"><span class="stonetop-holy-light-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
			{{/if}}
			{{/if}}
			{{! The Judge's scales, beside the candle and on the same terms — shown once they own
			    Condemn, or while brands are still standing on a sheet that has since lost the move,
			    so those can still be dismissed.

			    Always a <button>, where the candle is a button only where the sheet is editable.
			    That split is about who may WRITE, and this opens a list; reading who has been
			    branded is not an edit, and the dialog withholds its own add/dismiss controls from a
			    viewer who cannot write. `type="button"` is not optional: the whole sheet is one
			    <form> and a bare button submits it.

			    The count rides the button as a superscript rather than living only in the tooltip:
			    the one thing a Judge wants off this icon at a glance is how many brands are out
			    there, and a tooltip cannot be glanced at. Suppressed at zero — a Judge who has
			    branded nobody should see the scales, not a "0". }}
			{{#if stonetop.condemn.show}}
			<button type="button" class="stonetop-condemn{{#if stonetop.condemn.count}} is-branding{{/if}}"
			        aria-label="{{localize "stonetop.condemn.openLabel"}}"
			        data-tooltip="{{#if stonetop.condemn.count}}{{localize "stonetop.condemn.someTooltip" count=stonetop.condemn.count}}{{else}}{{localize "stonetop.condemn.noneTooltip"}}{{/if}}"
			        data-tooltip-direction="UP"><span class="stonetop-condemn-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{#if stonetop.condemn.count}}<span class="stonetop-condemn-count" aria-hidden="true">{{stonetop.condemn.count}}</span>{{/if}}</button>
			{{/if}}
		</div>
		{{! Through the Last Door, with no insert. The three returns say what they are in the name
		    at the top of the header (a Ghost reads "Ghost"), so only a plain death needs a word of
		    its own — and it is the one state the header could otherwise not tell from an ordinary
		    living character. It rides the end of the appearance line, which is the last thing said
		    about who this person is.

		    A BUTTON where the sheet can be edited: it opens "is this character being brought back?",
		    which is otherwise reachable only by putting hit points on a dead sheet — and a table
		    playing out a resurrection in the fiction first has no reason to have touched HP yet.
		    A plain span for anyone who can only look, so nothing offers a click that would do
		    nothing.

		    The `or` is not optional: the line only renders when there IS an appearance summary, and
		    a character who never filled one in would otherwise lose the tag entirely. The same is
		    true of the Condemned brand beside it, which is why that is in the guard too — a PC can
		    be Censured, and a branded one with no appearance written would have lost the mark.

		    This line is where the sheet keeps its tags about WHO THIS PERSON IS, which is why the
		    brand rides it rather than sitting by the name plate the way it does on the NPC and
		    monster sheets: those have no such line, and this one already carries Dead. }}
		{{#if (or stonetop.playbook.appearance.summary stonetop.isDead stonetop.condemned.condemned)}}
		<p class="stonetop-appearance-summary">{{stonetop.playbook.appearance.summary}}{{#if stonetop.isDead}}{{#if editable}}<button type="button" class="stonetop-dead-tag" data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.deadTooltipAction"}}" data-tooltip-direction="UP"><i class="fas fa-skull"></i>{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.deadTag"}}</button>{{else}}<span class="stonetop-dead-tag" data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.deadTooltip"}}" data-tooltip-direction="UP"><i class="fas fa-skull"></i>{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.deadTag"}}</span>{{/if}}{{/if}}{{#if stonetop.condemned.condemned}}{{> "stonetop.condemned-tag" byLabel=stonetop.condemned.byLabel}}{{/if}}</p>
		{{/if}}
	</div>
</div>
